WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.600
CNN's Ivan

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.034
Watson is

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.235
standing by in Hong Kong

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:04.471
with the latest from there Ivan.

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:06.272
China doubling down, issuing

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.074
some strong words after the U.S.

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:09.409
down the balloon.

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:10.410
That's right.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.812
Beijing is now saying that if the U.S.

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:13.947
essentially if the U.S.

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:15.782
flies a balloon over China,

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.150
it'll probably shoot it down.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:17.951
Look at this statement

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:20.020
coming from the Chinese defense ministry.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.287
Quote, The U.S.

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:22.455
used force to attack

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.224
our civilian unmanned airship,

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:26.459
which is an obvious overreaction.

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.161
We expressed solemn protest

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.896
against this move by the U.S.

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:32.232
side and reserve the right to use

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:33.500
necessary means

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.236
to deal with similar situations.

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:38.705
There has been a shift in the tone

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:39.906
from Beijing.

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:40.774
On Friday

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:42.675
evening, the Chinese foreign ministry

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:45.278
expressed regret, saying that it's

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.047
an air ship,

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:48.081
as it described it,

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:49.916
which was used primarily for research

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:50.717
purposes,

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:53.553
had blown off course over the U.S.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:56.122
And now the Chinese government,

00:00:56.156 --> 00:00:57.357
different ministries

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:59.859
are protesting the fact that that

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:00.794
this U.S.

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:03.496
fighter jet shot the balloon down.

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:05.632
The damage

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:06.032
on the

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:09.002
diplomatic front has already been visible

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:10.403
with the U.S.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:12.672
Secretary of State, Antony Blinken,

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:14.541
postponing a trip

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:15.141
that he was supposed

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:16.142
to make this weekend

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:19.145
to Beijing over this balloon scandal.

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:22.949
And calling the existence of this balloon

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:23.583
over U.S.

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:26.352
airspace a violation of U.S.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:29.089
sovereignty and of international law.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:30.990
The Chinese response has been,

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.859
hey, this is a weather.

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:33.827
This is due to weather.

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:35.728
It's out of our control.

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:37.297
They have been communicating

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:38.098
with their U.S.

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:40.667
counterparts but this has clearly done

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:41.734
some damage to

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:42.569
what was

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:43.103
an effort

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:44.504
that began in November

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:46.106
between President Biden

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.841
and the Chinese leader, Xi Jinping,

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:49.509
when they met face to face

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:51.578
at the G-20 summit in Bali

00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:52.946
to try to basically

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:53.980
put a stop

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.115
to the downward

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:56.616
spiral in relations

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:57.450
between the world's

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:58.985
two largest economies.

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.420
We'll just have to see

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.822
whether there can be any efforts to try

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:05.125
to revive diplomacy

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:07.660
in the wake of of this.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.662
I would argue a growing crisis.

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.499
How was this incident seen in the region?

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:14.701
Well, look,

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:19.005
it is creating a repercussion elsewhere.

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:20.640
The Canadian government

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.375
came out over the weekend

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:24.210
saying that this balloon

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.212
had been seen in Canadian airspace.

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:28.481
It summoned China's ambassador

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.183
to Ottawa then.

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:32.218
And now we're getting reports

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:33.987
of a second object

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:36.356
flying over Central and Latin America

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:37.590
that looks

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.626
remarkably similar to the balloon

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:42.428
that was just shot down over the U.S.

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:43.563
It was seen over

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:44.430
Costa Rica,

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.399
according to Costa Rican officials,

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:47.300
on Thursday.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.801
And then on Friday,

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.003
the Colombian Air Force

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:51.037
put out this statement

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:53.173
saying that this object

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:53.673
was seen

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:56.843
at an altitude of above 55,000 feet,

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:57.844
which is roughly

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.779
the same altitude as the balloon

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:01.381
that was seen over

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:02.582
the U.S.,

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:03.750
that it was monitored

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.186
and it was moving at a speed of 25 knots,

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:07.053
and that

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:09.889
the Colombians followed it until it left

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:11.658
Colombian airspace.

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:12.592
A U.S.

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:13.860
official telling CNN

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:14.661
they believe that

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:15.995
this also is,

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:17.730
as they put it, a Chinese

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.933
surveil launch balloon.

00:03:19.933 --> 00:03:21.100
We have put a question

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.569
in to the Chinese government

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:25.038
asking whether or not this is in fact

00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:27.473
a Chinese airship

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:29.943
as they've put it about, about the

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:30.810
the previous balloon

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:31.844
that was seen over U.S.

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.580
airspace. And also, U.S.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.881
officials have said

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:38.685
that they have also seen similar Chinese,

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:40.920
as they put it, surveillance balloons

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.589
three times over U.S.

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:44.891
airspace during the Trump administration

00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:47.460
and at least once over the U.S.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:50.463
earlier during the Biden administration.

00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:52.832
Why has this story to do this?

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:54.767
Why is this blown up this time?

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:55.702
Well, U.S.

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:57.904
officials say they haven't seen it

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.272
loitering over U.S.

00:03:59.272 --> 00:03:59.906
airspace

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:02.041
for such a duration of time in the past.

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:04.911
And we don't know that ordinary citizens

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:05.445
have been able

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.113
to see this kind of balloon

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:09.148
with their own eyes, with the naked eye

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:10.984
and take pictures of it before.

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:11.985
And that's part of what's

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:13.286
adding to the alarm here.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:15.989
Ivan Watson reporting from Hong Kong,

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:17.624
thanks so much. Ivan.

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:20.059
Mary Schiavo is a CNN

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:21.227
transportation analyst.

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:23.463
She joins us now from Anchorage, Alaska.

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:24.364
So good to see you.

00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:26.266
Mary, incidentally, the balloon

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:28.301
we understand, was first detected

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:30.603
last Saturday over Alaska.

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:32.872
It's now in the Atlantic Ocean

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:34.741
somewhere after quite a journey.

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:35.375
How long do

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:37.410
we expect to salvage operation to take

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:40.546
Well, actually, the United States

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:41.614
and several other countries

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:42.515
are very experienced

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:44.717
in these underwater salvage operations

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:47.787
because of downed aircraft over the past

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:49.055
and for many years.

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:50.790
And other underwater operations.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.592
So it's really going to depend upon

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:55.795
how lucky they are at finding the

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:58.331
the payload package, the debris.

00:04:58.331 --> 00:04:59.299
If you will, there

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:00.600
the equipment or whatever

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.235
fell from the balloon

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:04.404
and without what they call a pinger

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:06.072
many times or devices

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:07.407
that help you locate, for

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:08.608
example, black, black

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:10.410
boxes on down planes.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.211
But here, they don't expect to find that.

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:13.379
So they will just have

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:15.615
to literally scour the ocean floor.

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:18.751
But many of the world's nations are quite

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:20.086
experienced in underwater

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:21.754
recovery operations.

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:22.889
And, Mary, once

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:24.457
the parts are salvaged,

00:05:24.457 --> 00:05:26.793
will it be obvious whether investigators

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:28.695
are dealing with a spy and contraption

00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:29.796
or whether tracker?

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:31.230
Will that be obvious right away?

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:32.565
And what will they hope to learn

00:05:32.565 --> 00:05:33.499
by studying the balloon?

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:35.168
Well,

00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:36.369
it should be obvious,

00:05:36.369 --> 00:05:38.271
but then there's a big ifs here

00:05:38.271 --> 00:05:39.305
that depends upon

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:41.874
how well the equipment survived the fall

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:43.710
and how people think that water breaks

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:44.310
or fall.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:45.611
But literally from falling

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:47.146
from that height, it's

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:48.548
it's like hitting concrete.

00:05:48.548 --> 00:05:49.882
It's a very hard fall.

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:51.684
So they will have to see what is left

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:53.720
and what's there to determine,

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:55.455
which could, of course, be possible.

00:05:55.455 --> 00:05:56.589
They will have the equipment,

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:58.424
but they can't recover from it

00:05:58.424 --> 00:06:00.760
because of exposure to saltwater

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:02.528
or because of the impact.

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:04.530
But, yeah, the

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:05.765
you know, the United States

00:06:05.765 --> 00:06:06.666
and other countries

00:06:06.666 --> 00:06:08.000
that have experienced

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.369
an underwater recovery

00:06:09.369 --> 00:06:12.505
of aircraft parts and black boxes

00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:13.406
and equipment

00:06:13.406 --> 00:06:14.073
are pretty good

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:15.541
at downloading information

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:17.009
and putting it back together

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:19.412
because of investigators from prior

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:21.848
aviation accidents.

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:23.182
This isn't the first time

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:24.717
something like this has happened.

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:26.185
I understand that other suspected

00:06:26.185 --> 00:06:27.720
spy balloons have transited

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.122
across the continental U.S..

00:06:30.957 --> 00:06:31.524
That's right.

00:06:31.524 --> 00:06:32.592
They're reporting now.

00:06:32.592 --> 00:06:33.559
And and,

00:06:33.559 --> 00:06:33.793
you know,

00:06:33.793 --> 00:06:35.695
I think that the public sightings

00:06:35.695 --> 00:06:37.163
may play a big role in this.

00:06:37.163 --> 00:06:38.231
And what's happened this time?

00:06:38.231 --> 00:06:39.365
Because now

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:40.299
the government is saying

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:41.868
that this has been happening for

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:44.370
for as long as five or more years.

00:06:44.604 --> 00:06:46.005
There was one cited over

00:06:46.005 --> 00:06:49.108
Hawaii and Fabio sorry, of 20, 22

00:06:49.108 --> 00:06:50.343
just a year ago now.

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:51.611
The Costa Rica sighting.

00:06:51.611 --> 00:06:52.979
The Columbia sighting.

00:06:52.979 --> 00:06:55.581
So it's very difficult to

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:57.717
find that with the

00:06:57.717 --> 00:06:59.452
the story that it was just one

00:06:59.452 --> 00:07:00.953
balloon that escaped from China.

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:02.989
So I think that's part of

00:07:02.989 --> 00:07:03.723
the problem here

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:06.225
is too many to believe the explanation,

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:09.429
if it turns out to be a spying balloon,

00:07:09.429 --> 00:07:11.564
this still needs to be determined.

00:07:11.564 --> 00:07:13.566
Why use a brain for spying

00:07:13.566 --> 00:07:15.067
when you can use satellites?

00:07:15.067 --> 00:07:16.469
I mean, are they more effective?

00:07:16.469 --> 00:07:18.004
Because they're certainly not subtle

00:07:20.206 --> 00:07:20.706
Well, and

00:07:20.706 --> 00:07:23.709
the speculation and in the U.S.

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:24.811
and other circles

00:07:24.811 --> 00:07:26.212
and other places is, of course,

00:07:26.212 --> 00:07:27.547
they're searching for something.

00:07:27.547 --> 00:07:29.682
Satellites can't pick up

00:07:29.682 --> 00:07:32.985
other kinds of detection, communications

00:07:32.985 --> 00:07:36.022
signals, radiation signatures,

00:07:36.823 --> 00:07:38.958
other kinds of things that the satellites

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:40.460
can't possibly pick up.

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:42.261
So this would be a different

00:07:42.261 --> 00:07:44.530
kind of sensing equipment, most likely,

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:45.331
because if you're looking

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:46.933
for a visual sighting,

00:07:46.933 --> 00:07:48.901
obviously satellite

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:50.937
technology is so great that you can get,

00:07:51.204 --> 00:07:53.272
you know, pictures down to,

00:07:53.272 --> 00:07:55.308
you know, a few feet or in some cases

00:07:55.308 --> 00:07:56.075
a few inches.

00:07:56.075 --> 00:07:58.644
So that the technology on the satellites,

00:07:58.644 --> 00:08:00.246
if it's some kind of a visual

00:08:00.246 --> 00:08:02.482
sensing, is amazingly good.

00:08:02.482 --> 00:08:04.717
So the fact that some people speculate

00:08:04.717 --> 00:08:06.319
they were looking to locate US

00:08:06.319 --> 00:08:08.754
missile silos. Yeah, probably not.

00:08:08.788 --> 00:08:10.089
I'm sure they already know that.

00:08:10.089 --> 00:08:11.023
So this would be other

00:08:11.023 --> 00:08:12.558
kind of sensing equipment.

00:08:12.558 --> 00:08:14.494
And the speculation is most likely

00:08:14.494 --> 00:08:16.929
some kind of communications sensing

00:08:17.263 --> 00:08:19.131
radiation, microwave waves

00:08:19.131 --> 00:08:19.699
or other things

00:08:19.699 --> 00:08:21.167
that you could not readily sense

00:08:21.167 --> 00:08:22.902
from a satellite.

00:08:22.935 --> 00:08:24.403
And a final thought from you.

00:08:24.403 --> 00:08:25.137
Could Beijing

00:08:25.137 --> 00:08:26.939
ask to have the wreckage returned?

00:08:26.939 --> 00:08:27.907
I mean, what's the protocol

00:08:27.907 --> 00:08:29.108
in these situations?

00:08:29.108 --> 00:08:30.076
If there is a protocol?

00:08:31.611 --> 00:08:32.078
Well, you

00:08:32.078 --> 00:08:34.213
know, that kind of thing is

00:08:34.213 --> 00:08:35.715
that's very interesting question.

00:08:35.715 --> 00:08:37.216
And that has happened in the past.

00:08:37.216 --> 00:08:38.284
And the U.S.

00:08:38.284 --> 00:08:40.086
has been in similar situations

00:08:40.086 --> 00:08:41.687
where they have had

00:08:41.687 --> 00:08:44.223
heavy equipment, ships, planes, you name

00:08:44.223 --> 00:08:46.826
it, returned many, many years ago.

00:08:46.826 --> 00:08:48.861
Before, for many

00:08:48.861 --> 00:08:50.396
probably listening, were even born in

00:08:50.396 --> 00:08:52.098
the U.S., had a spy plane

00:08:52.098 --> 00:08:54.700
that was shot down. And, of course, U.S.

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:56.302
to ask to have it returned,

00:08:56.302 --> 00:08:58.271
they could ask to have it returned

00:08:58.271 --> 00:09:00.673
but when she was on the other foot

00:09:00.673 --> 00:09:01.474
and other

00:09:01.474 --> 00:09:03.609
countries, China, etc.,

00:09:03.609 --> 00:09:05.845
that equipment from the United States,

00:09:05.845 --> 00:09:06.212
you know,

00:09:06.212 --> 00:09:06.946
they didn't return

00:09:06.946 --> 00:09:08.147
and they certainly didn't return it

00:09:08.147 --> 00:09:10.049
until they saw what was on it.

00:09:10.049 --> 00:09:12.285
And because it did traverse the U.S.

00:09:12.318 --> 00:09:14.420
airspace, now they say, well, you know,

00:09:14.921 --> 00:09:17.490
you shot down a civilian aircraft,

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:18.391
not exactly.

00:09:18.391 --> 00:09:19.392
When you traverse

00:09:19.392 --> 00:09:20.960
the airspace of other countries,

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:22.061
there are treaties in place

00:09:22.061 --> 00:09:22.595
that govern

00:09:22.595 --> 00:09:24.564
that you have to give advice

00:09:24.564 --> 00:09:26.198
and permission, etc.

00:09:26.198 --> 00:09:27.733
And we don't have those same treaties

00:09:27.733 --> 00:09:29.335
in place with China, by the way.

00:09:29.335 --> 00:09:30.303
They're not the same

00:09:30.303 --> 00:09:31.771
for all countries of the world.

00:09:31.771 --> 00:09:34.240
So it did invade the airspace

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:35.174
without permission.

00:09:35.174 --> 00:09:36.542
And of course, the advisory

00:09:36.542 --> 00:09:38.144
that came too little too late

00:09:38.144 --> 00:09:39.145
doesn't explain that.

00:09:39.145 --> 00:09:41.280
So I think that the U.S.

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:42.148
will keep it.

00:09:43.516 --> 00:09:45.484
Mary Schiavo, I thank you so much.

00:09:45.484 --> 00:09:46.652
Greatly appreciate you. Thank you.

